    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14372" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dis-sĕco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dissĭc-</span></b> ), ŭi, ctum,
		1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to cut asunder</i>, <i>cut in
			pieces</i>, <i>cut up</i>, <i>dissect</i> (post-Aug.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">esp. freq. in Pliny the elder— cf.:
					seco, meto, findo, scindo): unionem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 35, 58, § 121</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 37, 70, § 185</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput viperae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					29, 4, 21, § 69</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mures,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					30, 9, 23, § 76</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ranas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					32, 9, 36, § 111</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multos medios serra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 27</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. M. 8, p.
			214</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dissecari cordibus suis,</span>”
				<i>to be cut to the heart</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act. 7, 54 al.</span></i>
			</div>
